\fs36 \cf0 This script applet will allow you to select a "dead" file track in iTunes (designated with the (!)) and attempt to locate a file using 
\f1\b Spotlight
\f0\b0  that corresponds to the selected track's Song Name, Artist, and Album, and then allow you to replace the "dead track" with a file from the search results. All tag data is preserved from the original track selected and copied to the newly added track.\
\

\f1\b Note
\f0\b0 : I consider this script to be just an experiment using Spotlight technology. iTunes already has the ability to try to locate disassociated files when you double-click a "dead track".\
